        "original_id": "654d8529-3d93-52ad-a988-0a04af45dd6c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Minnesota Twins\n- Places: Downtown East, Minneapolis; downtown Minneapolis; historic warehouse district; North Loop; Hubert H. Humphrey Metrodome; Target Field\n- Events: 2009 Minnesota Twins season; 2010 season\n\nFacts:\n- The 2009 Minnesota Twins season was the Minnesota Twins' final season at the Hubert H. Humphrey Metrodome.\n- Target Field opened in 2010 as the Minnesota Twins' new stadium.\n- At the start of the 2010 season, the Minnesota Twins moved into Target Field.\n- Target Field is a baseball park in the historic warehouse district, also called the North Loop, of downtown Minneapolis.",
